Tips & Tricks for Microsoft Word

Keyboard shortcut to add bullets in Word

When we want to list items or points in a text, we use bullets. Bullet poin=
ts allow us to summarise ideas and facts into short, neatly arranged senten=
ces.

=C2=A0

The usual way to add bullet points is to highlight the paragraph in which w=
e want to add bullet points and then choose our preferred style of numberin=
g from the home tab on the ribbon.

=C2=A0

However, Word has some shortcuts that can achieve the same thing.

LEARN THE SHORTCUTS ( https://www.simuldocs.com/blog/keyboard-shortcut-to-a=
dd-bullet-points-in-microsoft-word )

How to insert a PDF into a Word document

So you=E2=80=99ve found yourself with a PDF file that needs to be dropped i=
nto your working Microsoft Word Document but the old copy paste function ju=
st doesn=E2=80=99t seem to cut it.

=C2=A0

Maybe it's a reference file that you need to keep together with the Word do=
cument, or maybe you need it to actually be part of the Word document itsel=
f. There are many reasons you may be trying to insert a PDF into Word, so h=
ow is it done?

=C2=A0

The easiest way to insert your PDF file into Word is adding it as an =E2=80=
=98Object=E2=80=99, in this post we will show you how.

LEARN HOW TO INSERT A PDF ( https://www.simuldocs.com/blog/how-to-insert-a-=
pdf-into-a-microsoft-word-document )

How to change font kerning in Microsoft Word

Font kerning is the process of modifying the spacing between individual cha=
racters. Font kerning is usually done to achieve an aesthetically pleasing =
look to the text.=C2=A0

=C2=A0

There are a few different ways to do it in Microsoft Word, and in this arti=
cle we outline each way and when to use it.

LEARN ABOUT FONT KERNING ( https://www.simuldocs.com/blog/how-to-change-fon=
t-kerning-in-microsoft-word )

New Feature: A better way to collaborate outside Simul=C2=A0

One of the things we've learned about Simul users over hundreds of conversa=
tions is that not everybody they collaborate with actually has a Simul acco=
unt.

=C2=A0

It's always been possible to work with people outside of Simul and get thei=
r changes back into your version history, but it wasn't a great user experi=
ence. There were too many steps in the process and there were a number of w=
ays we could make it better.

=C2=A0

So we built a new feature called 'Share This Version' which makes it easier=
 and more secure to collaborate with people who don't have Simul accounts.

=C2=A0

To learn more about this new feature and how to use it, check out the launc=
h article.

LEARN THE NEW FEATURE ( https://www.simuldocs.com/announcements/share-this-=
version )

=C2=A0
